  <section class="section" id="istanbul-techniques">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header fade-in">
        <span class="label">By Technique</span>
        <h2>DHI and FUE in Istanbul</h2>
        <p>Both techniques are offered by almost every Istanbul clinic. The difference shows up in density, session limits and price.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="technique-grid">
        <div class="technique-card fade-in">
          <span class="badge badge-blue">DHI</span>
          <h3>DHI Hair Transplant in Istanbul</h3>
          <p>Follicles are extracted and implanted in one step with a Choi implanter pen, giving tight control over angle and depth. Istanbul clinics use it most often for hairlines, temple points and unshaven sessions where the graft count stays under about 3,000.</p>
          <ul class="technique-list">
            <li><strong>Typical range:</strong> 1,500 – 3,000 grafts</li>
            <li><strong>Cost for 3,000:</strong> $3,200 – $4,800</li>
            <li><strong>Shaving:</strong> partial or unshaven available</li>
            <li><strong>Strength:</strong> very high density in small areas</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="results.html?technique=dhi&amp;hospital=istanbul" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Actual DHI results →</a>
        </div>

        <div class="technique-card fade-in">
          <span class="badge badge-blue">FUE</span>
          <h3>FUE Hair Transplant in Istanbul</h3>
          <p>Grafts are harvested individually, channels are opened — often with a sapphire blade — and then implanted. It remains the workhorse technique in Istanbul because it handles large sessions covering the hairline, mid-scalp and crown in a single day.</p>
          <ul class="technique-list">
            <li><strong>Typical range:</strong> 2,000 – 4,500+ grafts</li>
            <li><strong>Cost for 3,000:</strong> $2,400 – $3,600</li>
            <li><strong>Shaving:</strong> full shave in most cases</li>
            <li><strong>Strength:</strong> broad coverage per session</li>
          </ul>
          <a href="results.html?technique=fue&amp;hospital=istanbul" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Actual FUE results →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- WHAT TO KNOW -->
  <section class="section" id="istanbul-checklist" style="background: #fff;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header fade-in">
        <span class="label">Before You Book</span>
        <h2>What to Know Before Choosing a Clinic</h2>
        <p>Istanbul has excellent surgeons and aggressive resellers in the same neighbourhood. These are the questions that separate them.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid-3">
        <div class="detail-card checklist-card fade-in">
          <span class="checklist-number">01</span>
          <h3>Who actually performs the surgery?</h3>
          <p>Ask by name which surgeon opens the channels and who implants the grafts. In high-volume clinics technicians do most of the work. That is not automatically bad, but it must be disclosed before you pay.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-card checklist-card fade-in">
          <span class="checklist-number">02</span>
          <h3>Is the graft number realistic?</h3>
          <p>A safe donor area rarely yields more than 4,000–5,000 grafts in one session. Quotes promising 6,000+ in a single day, or "unlimited grafts", usually count hairs rather than follicular units.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-card checklist-card fade-in">
          <span class="checklist-number">03</span>
          <h3>Do the photos match the patient?</h3>
          <p>Ask for cases with your hair type, loss pattern and age — photographed under the same lighting, at least 12 months apart. Consistency across many cases matters more than one dramatic transformation.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-card checklist-card fade-in">
          <span class="checklist-number">04</span>
          <h3>What does the package exclude?</h3>
          <p>Confirm in writing whether blood tests, medication, PRP sessions, the aftercare kit, hotel nights and airport transfers are included, and what a touch-up would cost if density falls short.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-card checklist-card fade-in">
          <span class="checklist-number">05</span>
          <h3>Is the clinic a licensed facility?</h3>
          <p>Procedures should take place in a Turkish Ministry of Health licensed hospital or surgical clinic, not a hotel room or an office. Ask for the licence and the operating surgeon's registration.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="detail-card checklist-card fade-in">
          <span class="checklist-number">06</span>
          <h3>How is follow-up handled?</h3>
          <p>You will be home during the months that matter. Agree who reviews your progress photos at 3, 6 and 12 months, on which channel, and whether a revision policy exists in writing.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PROCESS -->
  <section class="section" id="istanbul-process">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header fade-in">
        <span class="label">Step by Step</span>
        <h2>Hair Transplant Process in Istanbul</h2>
        <p>A typical Istanbul trip runs three to four days from landing to flying home, followed by a year of monitored growth.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-card fade-in" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <div class="blog-timeline">
          <div class="blog-timeline-item">
            <div class="blog-timeline-marker"></div>
            <div class="blog-timeline-content">
              <h4>1. Consultation — remote, 2 to 6 weeks before</h4>
              <p>You send photos of the front, top, crown and donor area. The clinic returns a hairline plan, an estimated graft range, a price and a list of blood tests. Compare at least three clinics on the plan itself, not only the price.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="blog-timeline-item">
            <div class="blog-timeline-marker"></div>
            <div class="blog-timeline-content">
              <h4>2. Arrival — day one</h4>
              <p>Airport transfer, hotel check-in, then an in-person examination. Donor density is measured, the hairline is drawn on your scalp and blood tests are run. This is the moment to adjust the design — after shaving it is too late.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="blog-timeline-item">
            <div class="blog-timeline-marker"></div>
            <div class="blog-timeline-content">
              <h4>3. Procedure — day two, 6 to 9 hours</h4>
              <p>Shaving, local anaesthesia, extraction, channel opening and implantation, with breaks for lunch. You stay awake throughout. Ask to see the graft count recorded at the end of the session.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="blog-timeline-item">
            <div class="blog-timeline-marker"></div>
            <div class="blog-timeline-content">
              <h4>4. Recovery — day three onward</h4>
              <p>First wash is demonstrated at the clinic, bandages are removed and PRP may be applied. Swelling peaks around days two to four, scabs clear within 10 to 14 days, and most patients are back at work inside a week.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="blog-timeline-item">
            <div class="blog-timeline-marker"></div>
            <div class="blog-timeline-content">
              <h4>5. Follow-up — month 3 to month 18</h4>
              <p>Shedding at weeks two to eight is expected. Real growth starts around month four, becomes convincing by month eight, and final density is judged at 12 to 18 months. Send progress photos on schedule so any shortfall is documented early.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="section" id="istanbul-faq" style="background: #fff;">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-header fade-in">
        <span class="label">FAQ</span>
        <h2>Istanbul Hair Transplant Questions</h2>
        <p>The questions patients ask most often before booking a trip to Istanbul.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="detail-card fade-in" style="max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <div class="faq-item active">
          <div class="faq-question">
            <span>Why is a hair transplant in Istanbul so much cheaper?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Lower staff and facility costs, a favourable exchange rate and very high procedure volume let Istanbul clinics charge a fraction of US or UK prices. The saving comes from the local cost base, not from cutting the number of grafts — but it also means the market is crowded, so verifying the surgeon matters more than in a smaller market.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-question">
            <span>How many days should I plan to stay?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Three to four nights is standard: arrival and examination on day one, surgery on day two, first wash and check-up on day three, then flying home. Add an extra night if you want the swelling to settle before travelling.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-question">
            <span>Should I choose DHI or FUE?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>It depends on the area being treated. DHI suits smaller, high-density zones such as the hairline and temples, and allows unshaven work. FUE handles larger sessions covering the mid-scalp and crown in one day at a lower price. A clinic that recommends the same technique to everyone is selling a package, not a plan.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-question">
            <span>Is the package price the final price?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Ask for a written breakdown before you travel. Blood tests, medication, PRP sessions, extra hotel nights and any future touch-up are the items most often excluded. Reputable clinics do not increase the price after the in-person examination unless the agreed graft range changes.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-question">
            <span>When will I see the final result?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Transplanted hairs shed within the first two months, regrowth becomes visible around month four, and density builds through month eight. Judge the outcome at 12 months for the hairline and up to 18 months for the crown. That is why every case in our gallery is labelled with its post-op timeline.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="faq-item">
          <div class="faq-question">
            <span>What happens if the result falls short?</span>
            <span class="faq-toggle">+</span>
          </div>
          <div class="faq-answer">
            <p>Established clinics offer a documented revision or touch-up policy, usually assessed at 12 months and often free of the surgical fee. Get the terms in writing before surgery and keep your own progress photos with dates, since they are the evidence any assessment relies on.</p>
          </div>
